&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The market is evolving, and we are too, moving the entire automotive journey online and guiding our customers through every step. That includes everything from the sale of an old car to the financing, purchase, and delivery of a new one. Today, tens of millions of consumers visit CarGurus.com each month, and ~30,000 dealerships use our products. But they&#39;re not the only ones who love CarGurus—our employees do, too. We have a people-first culture that fosters kindness, collaboration, and innovation, and empowers our Gurus with tools to fuel their career growth. Disrupting a trillion-dollar industry requires fresh and diverse perspectives. Come join us for the ride!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CarGurus is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Cloud FinOps Engineer II&lt;/strong&gt; to join the Cloud Enablement team and help establish FinOps as an engineering capability. This role will improve cloud cost visibility, attribution, governance, and optimization across Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll play a critical role in improving the accuracy and coverage of CarGurus’ cloud cost attribution, expanding self-service cost visibility, and helping engineering teams make informed decisions about cloud and AI spend. You’ll build automation and platform capabilities that establish repeatable anomaly-triage and savings workflows, support unit-cost metrics, and reduce the manual effort required to understand and optimize cloud consumption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain cloud cost attribution, tagging, and allocation capabilities across AWS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and improve CloudZero integrations, dashboards, reports, and data quality checks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop automation for cost anomaly detection, alerting, and investigation workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering, Product, Finance, and FinOps stakeholders to define useful unit-cost metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support showback and chargeback capabilities by improving ownership, service, team, and cost-center mappings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help establish FinOps checkpoints in the software development lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and automate cloud savings opportunities, including rightsizing, lifecycle management, Savings Plans, and Graviton adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to AI cost governance, including Bedrock usage visibility, token or inference cost attribution, budgets, and model-cost controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build self-service tools and documentation that allow engineering teams to answer cost questions independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write reliable Python, Go, Bash, Terraform, or similar automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in code reviews, incident response, operational support, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate findings clearly and turn analysis into actionable engineering recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of hands-on experience with AWS infrastructure, cloud cost management, or FinOps-related engineering in an enterprise environment. Experience may come from cloud infrastructure, platform engineering, or a dedicated FinOps role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting production workloads in AWS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Terraform and infrastructure automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python, Go, Bash, or another scripting language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of cloud cost concepts, including tagging, allocation, usage reporting, and anomaly detection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CloudZero, AWS Cost Explorer, CUR, or similar FinOps tooling is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with incomplete data and improve reporting accuracy over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A customer-focused approach to partnering with engineering and product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about AI infrastructure, model usage, and the economics of cloud services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with Finance or FP&amp;amp;A on cloud budgeting, forecasting, cost allocation, and business reporting is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;The displayed range represents the expected annual base salary / On-Target Earnings (OTE) for this position. On-Target Earnings (OTE) is inclusive of base salary and on-target commission earnings, which applies exclusively to sales roles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Individual pay within this range is determined by work location and other factors such as job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This annual base salary forms part of a comprehensive Total Rewards Package. In addition to benefits, this role may qualify for discretionary bonuses/incentives and Restricted Stock Units (RSUs).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Position Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$109,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$136,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Working at CarGurus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We reward our Gurus’ curiosity and passion with best-in-class benefits and compensation, including equity for all employees, both when they start and as they continue to grow with us. Our career development and corporate giving programs, as well as our employee resource groups (ERGs) and communities, help people build connections while making an impact in personally meaningful ways. A flexible hybrid model and robust time off policies encourage work-life balance and individual well-being. Thoughtful perks like daily free lunch, a new car discount, meditation and fitness apps, commuting cost coverage, and more help our people create space for what matters most in their personal and professional lives.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;CarGurus may require in-person interviews as part of our hiring process, particularly for positions based in our Boston and Dublin offices. Candidates selected for an in-person interview will be notified in advance. Please be aware that travel expenses are the responsibility of the candidate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We welcome all&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CarGurus strives to be a place to which people can bring the ultimate expression of themselves and their potential—starting with our hiring process. We do not discriminate based on race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, gender identity, or sexual orientation. We foster an inclusive environment that values people for their skills, experiences, and unique perspectives. That’s why we hope you’ll apply even if you don’t check every box listed in the job description. We also encourage you to tell your recruiter if you require accommodations to participate in our hiring process due to a disability so we can provide the appropriate support. We want to know what only you can bring to CarGurus. &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(236, 240, 241);&quot; data-lucid-type=&quot;application/vnd.lucid.text&quot; data-lucid-content=&quot;{&amp;quot;t&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Working at CarGurus \nWe reward our Gurus’ curiosity and passion with best-in-class benefits and compensation, including equity for all employees, both when they start and as they continue to grow with us. Our career development and corporate giving programs, as well as our employee resource groups (ERGs) and communities, help people build connections while making an impact in personally meaningful ways. A flexible hybrid model and robust time off policies encourage work-life balance and individual well-being. Thoughtful perks like daily free lunch, a new car discount, meditation and fitness apps, commuting cost coverage, and more help our people create space for what matters most in their personal and professional lives.&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;m&amp;quot;:[{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;a&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;p&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:1.1036906734302876},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;b&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;e&amp;quot;:19},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;c&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;#000000ff&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;e&amp;quot;:21},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:19.999999999999996,&amp;quot;e&amp;quot;:21},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:19,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;p&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:1.1036906734302876},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:21,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;a&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:21,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;p&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:1.1036906734302876},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:21,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;c&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;#1d1c1dff&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;e&amp;quot;:730},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:21,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:20,&amp;quot;e&amp;quot;:730}]}&quot;&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CarGurus (NASDAQ: CARG), our mission is to give people the power to reach their destination. We started as a small team of developers determined to bring trust and transparency to car shopping. Since then, our history of innovation and go-to-market acceleration has driven industry-leading growth. In fact, we’re the largest and fastest-growing automotive marketplace, and we’ve been profitable for over 15 years.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The market is evolving, and we are too, moving the entire automotive journey online and guiding our customers through every step. That includes everything from the sale of an old car to the financing, purchase, and delivery of a new one. Today, tens of millions of consumers visit CarGurus.com each month, and ~30,000 dealerships use our products. But they&#39;re not the only ones who love CarGurus—our employees do, too. We have a people-first culture that fosters kindness, collaboration, and innovation, and empowers our Gurus with tools to fuel their career growth. Disrupting a trillion-dollar industry requires fresh and diverse perspectives. Come join us for the ride!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Content Engineer to help operate and improve the systems and workflows that power CarGurus content.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a content-operations role with strong technical fluency. You will manage structured content in our headless CMS and related databases, coordinate multiple workflows for producing and updating content, and help ensure that every workflow produces accurate, useful, on-brand, and search-friendly work. You will work closely with editors, SEO partners, engineers, analysts, and other stakeholders to turn content requirements into repeatable processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You do not need to be a traditional software engineer. You should be comfortable learning technical systems, working with structured data, troubleshooting workflow issues, and using tools such as AirOps and LLM-based content workflows to improve the speed and quality of production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and maintain a structured database of content, including records, fields, statuses, metadata, templates, relationships, and update schedules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate day-to-day publishing and refresh workflows across multiple content types, markets, and production queues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate work from intake through review, revision, approval, publishing, and post-publication quality checks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and maintain Contentful models, entries, templates, and workflow states within established standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AirOps, LLM tools, and related AI-assisted workflows to support content creation, enrichment, updating, and quality control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review generated or data-informed content for accuracy, completeness, clarity, consistency, brand voice, and usefulness to car shoppers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor workflow output and investigate issues such as missing data, incorrect formatting, duplicate records, broken links, stale content, or failed production steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track answer-engine optimization (AEO) performance and citation visibility across AI and LLM search experiences; monitor where and how CarGurus content is cited, and use citation data to improve briefs, content structure, internal linking, prompts, and workflow outputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with editors and SEO stakeholders to translate briefs, content standards, and search intent into clear workflow requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain production trackers, documentation, QA checklists, and process guides so that work is visible, repeatable, and easy for others to follow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify recurring friction or quality issues and recommend practical improvements to templates, prompts, validations, queue design, and operating procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support testing of new content formats, data sources, and workflow changes; document results and help determine whether successful approaches should be expanded.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In your first year, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep assigned content databases accurate, organized, and up to date.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run multiple content-production and refresh workflows reliably against agreed timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Catch and resolve quality issues before they reach customers, or escalate them with clear context when they require another team’s support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the consistency, efficiency, or scalability of at least several recurring content processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trust with editorial, SEO, engineering, analytics, and other partners by communicating clearly and following work through to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the team increase content output without compromising accuracy, usefulness, differentiation, or brand standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in editorial operations, content operations, content management, publishing, SEO content, digital production, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical fluency and the ability to learn unfamiliar systems quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing structured content, databases, spreadsheets, CMS platforms, workflow tools, or production queues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A careful, methodical approach to data quality, content QA, and troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating multiple projects or workflows with competing deadlines and dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain technical or process issues to nontechnical partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good editorial judgment and a clear understanding of what makes content accurate, useful, readable, and consistent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with AI-assisted content tools while applying human review, fact checking, and quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work independently on varied, routine-to-moderately complex problems and to ask for help or escalate issues when appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Helpful experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contentful or another structured content management system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AirOps, LLM tools, prompt-based workflows, or other AI-assisted content-production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Content modeling, metadata management, taxonomy, templating, or database cleanup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SEO fundamentals, search intent, internal linking, structured data, or content performance reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Light scripting, spreadsheet automation, API-based workflows, or no-code/low-code tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with automotive content, ecommerce content, marketplace data, or other high-volume structured content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine interest in cars, automotive technology, or helping people make informed car-buying decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;The displayed range represents the expected annual base salary / On-Target Earnings (OTE) for this position. On-Target Earnings (OTE) is inclusive of base salary and on-target commission earnings, which applies exclusively to sales roles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Individual pay within this range is determined by work location and other factors such as job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This annual base salary forms part of a comprehensive Total Rewards Package. In addition to benefits, this role may qualify for discretionary bonuses/incentives and Restricted Stock Units (RSUs).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Position Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$64,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$81,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Working at CarGurus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
