&lt;p&gt;The market is evolving, and we are too, moving the entire automotive journey online and guiding our customers through every step. That includes everything from the sale of an old car to the financing, purchase, and delivery of a new one. Today, tens of millions of consumers visit CarGurus.com each month, and ~30,000 dealerships use our products. But they&#39;re not the only ones who love CarGurus—our employees do, too. We have a people-first culture that fosters kindness, collaboration, and innovation, and empowers our Gurus with tools to fuel their career growth. Disrupting a trillion-dollar industry requires fresh and diverse perspectives. Come join us for the ride!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CarGurus Canada is building a new Account Management team to create a more proactive, consultative, and customer-centered experience for dealer partners. The Manager, Account Management will be responsible for building and leading this team from the ground up, partnering with the Senior Director of Canada to build the operating model, hiring and developing talent, and driving strong retention, adoption, and growth outcomes across the Canadian dealer base.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This leader will oversee Account Managers supporting high-volume and lower-complexity accounts all the way to growth-oriented single rooftops and multi-store groups, and strategic national and multi-rooftop partnerships. The manager will ensure that each segment receives the right level of engagement, analysis, coaching, and commercial support while creating clear alignment across Account Management, Account Executives, Dealer Relations, and Canada sales leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is an experienced people leader and builder who is comfortable making decisions in an evolving environment, while working heavily with their peers. They bring a strong point of view, extensive hiring experience, sound judgment, test new approaches, and continuously improve the team and its processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and lead the Canada Account Management function&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the build out of the Account Management team, supporting creation of roles, responsibilities, service expectations, and rules of engagement between Account Managers + Account Executives, with the Senior Director of Canada and supporting team leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create scalable processes for account planning, customer engagement, performance reviews, churn mitigation, opportunity generation, and Salesforce documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make thoughtful, timely decisions about team structure, prioritization, resource allocation, and customer coverage as the business evolves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hire, coach, and develop a high-performing team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring extensive hiring experience and a demonstrated ability to identify, attract, and select strong talent across different levels of Account Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a team culture grounded in customer centricity, accountability, collaboration, continuous learning, and high standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear expectations and development plans for Account Managers at every level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach team members through regular one-on-ones, call and account-plan reviews, performance feedback, and career conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide direct, timely, and actionable feedback while recognizing strong performance and addressing performance gaps fairly and consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive customer and business outcomes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the team in owning dealer success, product adoption, retention, and growth throughout the customer lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Account Managers to deliver the right level of engagement across dealer segments—from efficient, proactive high-volume coverage and churn mitigation, to consultative partnerships that demonstrate CarGurus ROI and drive adoption and expansion, to strategic, insight-led engagement for high-value and complex dealership groups through executive relationships, performance reviews, success plans, and proactive save motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate team performance and KPI’s, using relevant data to identify risk, measure impact, improve coverage, guide decisions, and balance customer outcomes, engagement quality, retention, and growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encourage partnership with Account Executives to identify and qualify cross-sell, upsell, renewal, and revenue-recapture opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the team navigate complex churn conversations, cancellations, contract questions, escalations, billing issues, technical issues, and product adoption challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong working relationships with cross functional teams to resolve issues and improve the dealer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 2 years of experience leading, coaching, and developing a customer-facing sales, account management, customer success, or client services team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience hiring and building teams, evaluating talent, making hiring decisions, and onboarding new employees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of improving retention, customer engagement, adoption, expansion, or other measurable customer and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to coach across a range of account segments, from high-volume transactional coverage to complex, executive-level partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, presentation, and stakeholder-management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness to evolve, experiment, receive feedback, provide feedback, and change course when the evidence supports a better approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work collaboratively with the Director of Canada and existing Canada leaders while also taking ownership and moving work forward independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;The displayed range represents the expected annual base salary / On-Target Earnings (OTE) for this position. On-Target Earnings (OTE) is inclusive of base salary and on-target commission earnings, which applies exclusively to sales roles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Individual pay within this range is determined by work location and other factors such as job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This annual base salary forms part of a comprehensive Total Rewards Package. In addition to benefits, this role may qualify for discretionary bonuses/incentives and Restricted Stock Units (RSUs).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Position Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$136,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$175,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Working at CarGurus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We reward our Gurus’ curiosity and passion with best-in-class benefits and compensation, including equity for all employees, both when they start and as they continue to grow with us. Our career development and corporate giving programs, as well as our employee resource groups (ERGs) and communities, help people build connections while making an impact in personally meaningful ways. A flexible hybrid model and robust time off policies encourage work-life balance and individual well-being. Thoughtful perks like daily free lunch, a new car discount, meditation and fitness apps, commuting cost coverage, and more help our people create space for what matters most in their personal and professional lives.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;CarGurus may require in-person interviews as part of our hiring process, particularly for positions based in our Boston and Dublin offices. Candidates selected for an in-person interview will be notified in advance. Please be aware that travel expenses are the responsibility of the candidate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We welcome all&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CarGurus strives to be a place to which people can bring the ultimate expression of themselves and their potential—starting with our hiring process. We do not discriminate based on race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, gender identity, or sexual orientation. We foster an inclusive environment that values people for their skills, experiences, and unique perspectives. That’s why we hope you’ll apply even if you don’t check every box listed in the job description. We also encourage you to tell your recruiter if you require accommodations to participate in our hiring process due to a disability so we can provide the appropriate support. We want to know what only you can bring to CarGurus. &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(236, 240, 241);&quot; data-lucid-type=&quot;application/vnd.lucid.text&quot; data-lucid-content=&quot;{&amp;quot;t&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Working at CarGurus \nWe reward our Gurus’ curiosity and passion with best-in-class benefits and compensation, including equity for all employees, both when they start and as they continue to grow with us. Our career development and corporate giving programs, as well as our employee resource groups (ERGs) and communities, help people build connections while making an impact in personally meaningful ways. A flexible hybrid model and robust time off policies encourage work-life balance and individual well-being. Thoughtful perks like daily free lunch, a new car discount, meditation and fitness apps, commuting cost coverage, and more help our people create space for what matters most in their personal and professional lives.&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;m&amp;quot;:[{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;a&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;p&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:1.1036906734302876},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;b&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;e&amp;quot;:19},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;c&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;#000000ff&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;e&amp;quot;:21},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:19.999999999999996,&amp;quot;e&amp;quot;:21},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:19,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;p&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:1.1036906734302876},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:21,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;a&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:21,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;p&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:1.1036906734302876},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:21,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;c&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;#1d1c1dff&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;e&amp;quot;:730},{&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;:21,&amp;quot;n&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;s&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;v&amp;quot;:20,&amp;quot;e&amp;quot;:730}]}&quot;&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CarGurus (NASDAQ: CARG), our mission is to give people the power to reach their destination. We started as a small team of developers determined to bring trust and transparency to car shopping. Since then, our history of innovation and go-to-market acceleration has driven industry-leading growth. In fact, we’re the largest and fastest-growing automotive marketplace, and we’ve been profitable for over 15 years.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The market is evolving, and we are too, moving the entire automotive journey online and guiding our customers through every step. That includes everything from the sale of an old car to the financing, purchase, and delivery of a new one. Today, tens of millions of consumers visit CarGurus.com each month, and ~30,000 dealerships use our products. But they&#39;re not the only ones who love CarGurus—our employees do, too. We have a people-first culture that fosters kindness, collaboration, and innovation, and empowers our Gurus with tools to fuel their career growth. Disrupting a trillion-dollar industry requires fresh and diverse perspectives. Come join us for the ride!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CarGurus is hiring an Engineering Manager to lead the Purchase team within our Consumer Engineering department. The Purchase team owns the consumer journey from the moment a shopper decides on a car to the moment the deal is done. That means delivering an experience that meets consumers where they are—whether they want agents to handle the heavy lifting on their behalf, or prefer to be guided through each step of financing, trade-in, and deal configuration themselves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a pivotal leadership role at an exciting moment: we are actively transitioning our engineering practices toward AI-native and fully agentic development, and this manager will be a key driver of that transformation. You&#39;ll lead a team of talented engineers, shape the technical vision for one of our most strategically important product areas, and champion AI-forward ways of working—from integrating AI coding assistants into daily workflows to architecting intelligent, consumer-facing experiences. If you&#39;re energized by the intersection of modern AI development and high-impact consumer products, this is the role for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor, and grow a team of engineers, supporting their technical development and career growth while fostering a collaborative, high-performance team culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product, UX, and Analytics to drive the Purchase roadmap from concept through technical design, implementation, testing, and measurement; actively contribute to roadmap prioritization by proposing technical investments and providing well-reasoned estimates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion AI-forward engineering practices across the team—actively promoting the use of AI coding assistants, agentic workflows, and AI-driven tooling as core parts of the development process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the team&#39;s transition to fully agentic programming paradigms, setting expectations, removing blockers, and modeling the mindset shift required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive delivery of consumer-facing AI experiences, collaborating with product and design to bring intelligent, personalized features to millions of car shoppers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage project scope, estimation, and prioritization; decompose complex initiatives into small, self-contained units of work and drive their incremental delivery with a bias toward shipping and learning quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate effectively across team boundaries—working with consumer, dealer, and platform engineering teams to align on dependencies, define integration requirements, and ensure the Purchase platform evolves reliably alongside the broader CarGurus ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Roll up your sleeves and pitch in wherever you&#39;ll have the greatest impact—whether that&#39;s diving into a technical design session, helping scope an A/B test, unblocking a critical dependency, or jumping into any other area where your involvement moves the team forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for engineering excellence—code quality, observability, system reliability, and continuous improvement in process and tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have fun!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of relevant engineering experience, with 3+ years in an engineering management or technical lead role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid backend engineering foundation—comfortable engaging deeply in architectural discussions, system design, and technical trade-offs, particularly in Java/Spring environments, distributed systems, and data layer design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine enthusiasm for AI and agentic development: you believe AI coding tools and multi-agent workflows are the future of software engineering, and you lead by example in adopting them—set a vision for AI-native development practices and guide engineers through the cultural and technical shift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering consumer-facing AI features or products; experience with conversational or agentic AI experiences is a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer and product-focused mindset with a bias toward data-driven decisions, and a track record of shipping high-quality, user-centric features at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills and experience with Agile methodologies; able to drive clarity and incremental progress in fast-moving, ambiguous environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to mentor engineers and help them grow technically and professionally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator and collaborator who builds trust across engineering, product, and design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious, empathetic, and plays well with others—with a commitment to continuous learning and expanding your capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;The displayed range represents the expected annual base salary / On-Target Earnings (OTE) for this position. On-Target Earnings (OTE) is inclusive of base salary and on-target commission earnings, which applies exclusively to sales roles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Individual pay within this range is determined by work location and other factors such as job-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This annual base salary forms part of a comprehensive Total Rewards Package. In addition to benefits, this role may qualify for discretionary bonuses/incentives and Restricted Stock Units (RSUs).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Position Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$186,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$233,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Working at CarGurus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We reward our Gurus’ curiosity and passion with best-in-class benefits and compensation, including equity for all employees, both when they start and as they continue to grow with us. Our career development and corporate giving programs, as well as our employee resource groups (ERGs) and communities, help people build connections while making an impact in personally meaningful ways. A flexible hybrid model and robust time off policies encourage work-life balance and individual well-being. Thoughtful perks like daily free lunch, a new car discount, meditation and fitness apps, commuting cost coverage, and more help our people create space for what matters most in their personal and professional lives.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;CarGurus may require in-person interviews as part of our hiring process, particularly for positions based in our Boston and Dublin offices. Candidates selected for an in-person interview will be notified in advance. Please be aware that travel expenses are the responsibility of the candidate.&lt;/p&gt;
