&lt;p&gt;CarGurus is hiring for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Principal Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; in our Consumer Commerce department – the group responsible for our highest trafficked pages and products. Our mission is to deliver comprehensive, accurate, and engaging vehicle information, fostering trust and driving informed and high-intent consumer decisions, while upholding CarGurus’ standards for innovation, user-centricity, and technical excellence.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll contribute to high‑visibility parts of our site, introduce AI to our consumer experiences, and collaborate closely with partners in Product, UX, and Analytics. This is a fast-moving, impact-oriented environment where you will set technical direction across the department, mentor engineers, and drive high-visibility AI initiatives from concept to production at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and deploy consumer-facing experiences end-to-end to 45 million monthly visitors, from the data and model layer through to the user-facing product, being hands-on and actively participating in the implementation of select initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a go-to AI expert and advisor for all Consumer AI projects, providing technical guidance on architecture, design, and implementation choices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the platform and infrastructure decisions underpinning AI deployments, including storage, memory, request handling and load, evaluation pipelines, observability and analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate the broader AI framework and tooling landscape, independent of any single language or ecosystem, and guide teams toward the right approach for a given problem; develop proof-of-concepts to validate AI approaches and clearly explain the trade-offs between different technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and operate systems using LangChain, LangGraph, and Langfuse in Python to develop, orchestrate, and evaluate agentic and LLM-based applications in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the department&#39;s adoption of fully agentic programming, defining the patterns, tooling, and best practices engineers follow when building agentic systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering leadership, product, and data teams to shape phased platform guidelines and roadmaps for consumer initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers across teams on system design, evaluation methodology, and operational best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct workshops and produce documentation on AI development, deployment, monitoring, and support practices across multiple teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document architectural decisions in Architecture Decision Records (ADRs) and share findings and best practices across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience architecting resilient, scalable systems and leading technical direction across multiple teams with extensive experience designing, implementing, and deploying consumer-facing AI experiences in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with LangChain, LangGraph, and LangFuse in Python and with the platform and infrastructure layers of AI systems, including storage, memory, load management, evaluations, and observability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad knowledge of the AI framework and tooling landscape beyond Python, with the ability to evaluate and recommend approaches independent of language or ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on full stack experience building well-structured, performant applications across frontend, backend, and the platform and infrastructure layers for production-grade systems, including experience building APIs and REST services in Java and UX applications in React preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator with a collaborative spirit who can influence technical direction across multiple teams and disciplines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working within the AWS ecosystem a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with agentic programming and multi-agent workflows, including guiding teams through adoption of these approaches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining engineering patterns and standards that others adopt, and mentoring engineers on architecture and coding practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
